From fe7e9d698acb636fa5fe54ca1f9211713026e0b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:51:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 59/91] ggml-cuda : the fused gate/up GEMV + GLU epilogue takes
 GGML_GLU_OP_SWIGLU_LIM (SiegeLadder G8, decode half)

With V4's clamps folded into one GLU op (70fc66d) the pattern MUL_MAT(_ID) gate, MUL_MAT(_ID) up, GLU matches the
fused mmvq / mmvf path: the epilogue applies ggml_cuda_op_swiglu_lim_single with the GLU's limit (op_params[2], carried
as glu_param in the fusion args). A wave's ids variant (src[2]) stays unfused. test-backend-ops: MUL_MAT_VEC_FUSION
with SWIGLU_LIM (144 cases), 504 / 504.

SiegeLadder (o35, o36): bitwise - decode exact path against the 17.10 KL base KLD 0.00000, PPL x1.0000; exact
without runahead text = trace and o32's counters to the unit. Speed: the default mode 14.856 vs 14.867 tok/s (ABBA x2,
sd 0.39; the time outside the drive wait 40.22 vs 40.41 ms), exact runahead 14.16 vs 14.31 - within noise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
